{"session_id":"a9c8ca57-1c71-4ffc-8cd5-58a9aa5b0b58","transcript_path":"/Users/paul.grimshaw/.claude/projects/-Users-paul-grimshaw-dev-remit-fresh/a9c8ca57-1c71-4ffc-8cd5-58a9aa5b0b58.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/paul.grimshaw/dev/remit-fresh","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"Stop","stop_hook_active":false,"last_assistant_message":"**🎯 We found it. Linkage is solved — and it's even simpler than expected.**\n\nIn scout's `SessionStart` payload, the env vars contain:\n\n```\nCLAUDE_SESSION_ID=a9c8ca57-1c71-4ffc-8cd5-58a9aa5b0b58   ← this is the PARENT'S session_id\nCLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR=/Users/paul.grimshaw/dev/remit-fresh\nCLAUDE_ENV_FILE=/Users/paul.grimshaw/.claude/session-env/6afd4fc6.../sessionstart-hook-1.sh\n```\n\nAnd just to triple-confirm, scout's parent `claude` process has all of this in its **argv**:\n\n```\nppid: 67902  .../claude/versions/2.1.126\n                --agent-id scout@diag\n                --agent-name scout\n                --team-name diag\n                --parent-session-id a9c8ca57-1c71-4ffc-8cd5-58a9aa5b0b58\n                --agent-type general-purpose\n                --model claude-opus-4-7\n```\n\nSo we have **three independent linkage channels**, in order of simplicity:\n\n1. **`CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` env var** — set by Claude Code in spawned team-member processes; its value IS the parent's session_id. **Top-level sessions don't have it set.** 3 lines of Rust to read.\n2. **`--parent-session-id` flag in ppid's argv** — same info, harder to read, but a fallback if env is ever stripped.\n3. **Process tree + `--session-id`** — what we'd need if the above two were unavailable. Not needed.\n\nPlus we get free metadata: `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`, `--agent-id` (`scout@diag`), `--team-name`, `--agent-type`. All readable, all set by Claude Code, none model-controllable.\n\n## What this means for v1\n\nThe hook adapter just needs:\n\n```rust\nlet parent_session_id = std::env::var(\"CLAUDE_SESSION_ID\").ok();\n```\n\nMap it into the domain (e.g. add `parent_session_id: Option<String>` to `ClassificationInput`) and `resolve_scope` walks the chain: if I have a parent, look up parent's scope. **No PPID inspection, no sysctl, no daemon needed.**\n\nThis works for both topologies:\n- In-process Agent (same `session_id` as parent): `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` is unset → no parent inference needed; same scope by virtue of same session.\n- Team peer-session (different `session_id`): `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` is set to parent's → child inherits via lookup.\n\n## Other things noted from the dump\n\n- `SubagentStart` / `SubagentStop` events did **NOT** fire for the team-member spawn — only `SessionStart` / `SessionEnd`. So those names are reserved for in-process subagents only (or aren't yet emitted; either way, can't rely on them for teams).\n- The team member's `transcript_path` is right there in the payload — useful if we ever want to read its conversation log.\n- `permission_mode` is on every payload (`\"default\"`).\n- 27 dump events from a tiny test, totalling ~1600 lines. Nice density.\n\n---\n\n## Sanitizing for the repo\n\nYou said you want to store these as diagnostic reference. Items to scrub before committing:\n- `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<REDACTED>


